# Battle Core Mechanics

## Node Control System [to-do]
- Strategic network nodes (specifically nodes 3, 4, and 5) must be captured and held
- Node capture threshold set at 75% of total battalion health from both sides
- Capture progress shown with team colors (red/blue)
- Track accumulated damage per side using zero-sum system
- Opponents must first negate existing progress before gaining control

## Network Bonus System [to-do]
- When node is captured, connected network lines glow with team color
- For example: if node 3 is captured, lines to nodes 0, 1, 6, and 7 would glow
- Battalions on glowing network lines receive 2% bonus to all stats (attack, defense, speed, range)
- Visual indicator shows which battalions are receiving bonus
- Bonus updates immediately when node control changes

## Loss Tracking System [to-do]
- Tracks battalion losses by quantity
- Records mark level of lost units (Mk1-4)
- Calculates point values based on mark (Mk1=1pt, Mk2=2pts, Mk3=4pts, Mk4=8pts)
- Updates loss counter in real-time
- Provides summary for battle conclusion

## Battle Timer System [to-do]
- Implement precise 20-second battle timer
- Countdown phase before battle begins
- Active battle phase during 20-second timer
- Conclusion phase when timer expires
- All movement and actions stop at timer expiration

## Scoring System [to-do]
- Points awarded for:
  - Enemy battalion elimination (based on mark level)
  - Node control
  - Battle duration survival
- Higher score determines victor
- Tie-breaking: defending party wins ties

## Victory Determination [to-do]
- Victory achieved through:
  - Total control of nodes 3, 4, and 5
  - Point threshold reached
  - Enemy force elimination
  - Battle timer expiration (highest score wins)
- Apply tie-breaking when scores are equal

## Initial Targeting System [to-do]
- At battle start, battalions randomly target one of nodes 3, 4, or 5
- Only nodes 3, 4, and 5 can be targeted for capture
- While moving, check for closer targets continuously
- Once attacking, maintain target until conditions change
- Retarget when current target is destroyed/captured/moved

## Movement and Pathfinding [to-do]
- Calculate paths along network lines using A* algorithm
- Battalion speed determines movement time (fastest reach nodes in 2-3 seconds)
- Stop movement when attack range reaches target
- Different battalion types have different attack ranges
- No retreat functionality - always advance toward objectives

## Combat System [to-do]
### Damage Calculation:
- Total attack power = base_offense * battalion_quantity
- Defense reduction: damage = attack * (1 - defense/100)
- Minimum damage of 1 point
- Individual battalion total health tracking
- Damage application after defense calculation
- Destruction at 0 total health

## State Management System [to-do]
### Core Principles:
- Single source of truth
- Centralized state management
- Clear ownership of state updates
- Predictable state transitions
- Atomic state operations

### Update Frequency:
- Optimize update timing for smooth user experience
- Batch related state changes
- Prioritize visual responsiveness
- Handle state dependencies efficiently

## Update Timing System [to-do]
### Three-tier hierarchy:
1. Real-time:
   - Animations, movement, visual effects
   - Smooth, responsive visual feedback

2. Speed-based:
   - Attack animations (per battalion speed stat)
   - Movement based on battalion speed stat
   - Fastest battalions reach nodes in 2-3 seconds

3. Global timer:
   - Health, damage, state synchronization
   - Score and progress updates
   - 20-second battle duration tracking

## MVP Implementation Focus
- Prioritize smooth user experience
- Focus on core gameplay mechanics
- Implement essential visual feedback
- Ensure battles properly conclude with clear outcome
- Balance simplicity with strategic depth

